equivalent SUMMARY checks=408 failures=0
the character allowlist refuses a superset of what the two address grammars refuse, so deleting the loop cannot change a parse outcome. Harness.clientAddress sweeps 20 564 strings the allowlist refuses -- every non-allowlisted character on its own and at every position of eleven address seeds, plus every short string that mixes them with grammar characters -- and asserts none of them reaches a bucket. Running this mutant, that section reports failures=0: with the loop gone every one of the 20 564 strings is still refused by the grammars, which is the equivalence. If a grammar is ever loosened the sweep fails and this entry has to go.
